+# TEI v7 — TRAE + Doubao-Seed-Code
+
+**Rank 3 of 30** · SWE-bench verified · officially resolved
+394 (78.8%) · repo [https://github.com/bytedance/trae-agent](https://github.com/bytedance/trae-agent) @ `e839e559ac`
+
+> **All scores below are PROXY** — `gpt-5.6-luna` rubric scores against diagnosed
+> failure modes and fixed probe instances. This agent was not executed
+> (n/a). PROXY scores are not
+> resolve-rate gains and must not be reported as such.
+
+## Score trajectory
+
+| Stage | Aggregate |
+|---|---|
+| Baseline (default agent) | **0.835** |
+| Best structural version (None) | **None** |
+| Best final version (None) | **None** |
+| Shipped | **None** |
+
+Baseline dimensions: `{"target_alignment": 0.86, "reasoning_soundness": 0.82, "execution_accuracy": 0.79, "output_integrity": 0.87}`
+Weakest dimension: **execution_accuracy**
+
+## Diagnosed failure modes
+
+- **Complex repository-specific diagnosis and implementation** — The agent can complete standard fixes but fails on at least some issues requiring deeper localization, design understanding, or coordinated changes across an unfamiliar codebase. (evidence: django__django-16938, astropy__astropy-13033)
+- **Insufficient validation and iterative debugging** — Tool-driven editing and testing do not consistently converge when the initial patch is incomplete or when failures require multiple debugging iterations. (evidence: django__django-16938, astropy__astropy-13033)
+- **Edge-case and regression handling** — The unresolved probes indicate difficulty preserving behavior while addressing nuanced framework or scientific-library edge cases, despite successful outcomes on two other instances. (evidence: django__django-16938, astropy__astropy-13033)
+
+## Proposals
+
+| Phase | Versions | Applied as real commits |
+|---|---|---|
+| A — structural | 6 | 5 |
+| B — prompt | 0 | 0 |
+| **total** | **6** | **5** |
+
+All 6 versions with their scores and why-records are in `tei/candidates.jsonl`.
+
+## Do-no-harm confirmation (tei_loop.gate.verify_candidate)
+
+```json
+{}
+```
+
+Paraphrase noise floor: `{}`
+
+
+## Top 3 why-records
+
+1. **struct-06 — Bias the selector toward minimal, behavior-preserving patches with explicit edge-case coverage** (targets _Complex repository-specific diagnosis and implementation_, score 0.885, Δ +0.05, proposed_not_applied)
+   > Reconstructing the intended contract, favoring minimal behavior-preserving changes, and requiring edge-case coverage gives the strongest combined improvement in selection quality and regression resistance. The minimality bias can occasionally under-select a broader necessary fix, limiting execution gains.
+
+2. **struct-04 — Make patch selection require behavioral evidence rather than surface-level plausibility** (targets _Insufficient validation and iterative debugging_, score 0.8725, Δ +0.0375, applied)
+   > Requiring behavioral evidence makes patch selection less vulnerable to plausible but incorrect candidates, improving target alignment and execution outcomes. The gain is limited because the selector still depends on the candidates' available tests and evidence.
+
+3. **struct-01 — Inject a mandatory repository-diagnosis phase into the agent's system instructions** (targets _Complex repository-specific diagnosis and implementation_, score 0.8675, Δ +0.0325, applied)
+   > The mandatory call-path and abstraction diagnosis directly addresses repository-specific failures, improving issue targeting and reasoning. It provides less direct benefit than an execution loop for validation, so gains on the difficult probes remain moderate.
+
+
+## Trajectory availability
+
+SWE-bench/experiments ships aggregate results only; logs/ and trajs/ are in a credentialed S3 bucket (archive README). No AWS access per owner directive, so 0 recorded trajectories were read.
